.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt PASTE 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm paste
.Nd combine lines from files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s
.Op Fl d Ar delimiters
.Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Read one line from each file and print the lines side by side separated by tabs.
A file that ends early contributes empty fields until every input ends.
A dash names standard input.
With
.Fl s ,
join the lines of each file into one output line.
With
.Fl d ,
cycle through the given delimiter characters instead of tabs.
The escapes for newline, tab, backslash and a zero delimiter are supported.
The zero delimiter (\e0) emits a NUL byte between columns in parallel mode;
in sequential mode it inserts nothing. An empty delimiter list is refused.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Zero on success, nonzero on input, output or usage errors.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
paste /home/operator/left /home/operator/right
paste -s -d , /home/operator/left
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cut 1 ,
.Xr sbase 7
